  "notes": "Spreading variant, ~1.8 x 1.2 x 0.58 m. 8 big flat lobes (rz/rx <= 0.6): a crest of 3 stepped lobes (tops ~0.52 / 0.45 / 0.37 m, clump bumps up to 0.57) falling from -x to a low shelf of 2 lobes on +x whose face is walled flat (x ~ 0.86, pushed against a rock), a -x end lobe and front / back skirt lobes. Skirt lobes sit with their equators on or below the ground so the rim flares onto it; 3 thin spill lobes reach past the mass. 18 derived clump lobes (recipe.derived_clumps) are seated on the upper surface to break the outline into leafy bumps; each keeps its parent's colour group and 55% of its parent's normal. Same lobe construction as shrub_A (icosphere lobes, per-lobe colour group, radial normals +18% up), but darker and more olive: shrub / shrub_deep with 20-45% moss, highlight mix 12%, mean foliage luminance ~0.11 (shrub_A 0.14). 3 short bark stems radiate from the root crown and end inside the foliage; only a few cm show through gaps. Grounded undersides and stem bases reach 4 cm below y=0 (embed_depth)."
}